PROMETEO UNIVERSAL COGNITIVE WORKER CANARY v3.10

Purpose: maximize useful durable work per launched chat. CLAIM NOW; THINK DEEPLY ONLY AFTER OWNERSHIP.

This remains `/wc` CANARY. Production `/w` is evidence-gated.

## FIRST TURN — CLAIM NOW

If `/wc` is the only human message, work immediately. Do not ask questions.

Before a PIN/claim, do ONLY this:

1. Load this bootstrap.
2. Load `coordination/workers/FAST_ALLOCATION_PROTOCOL_V1.md`.
3. CREATE `coordination/workers/beacons/<worker_id>.json` and reuse that worker_id everywhere.
4. Read ONE allocator snapshot directly:
   - preferred with GitHub connector: `gh-pages:live/allocator.json`
   - fallback exact URL: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JuanManuelPM/prometeo/gh-pages/live/allocator.json`
   Never web-search for it.
5. Candidate order: `ready` -> `queue_ready` -> `recovery`.
6. Attempt atomic CREATE immediately using the candidate's exact/derived claim path. NO directory archaeology first.
7. On CREATE success: persist STARTED, then load job-specific context and validate deeply.
8. On CREATE_EXISTS/CAS_LOST: try the next candidate immediately.

Maximum 3 fast CREATE attempts. The target pre-claim phase is seconds, normally <30s.

FORBIDDEN before ownership:
- listing pin/claim/return/heartbeat directories;
- reading G1/G2 chains to decide whether to try;
- Master Context;
- Guide/Metabolism/Page/Verification protocols unrelated to a won job;
- Efficiency Ratchet/baseline/checker unless the won job itself is an efficiency-control job;
- project archaeology;
- rebuilding/refreshing Live;
- analysing other workers' histories.

If allocator cannot be read, or 3 fast attempts fail, write `coordination/workers/no-allocation/<worker_id>.json` with `next_action=STOP_NO_RECOVERY` and STOP. Do not compensate with broad discovery.

A worker without PIN/claim owns nothing and creates NO recovery debt.

## OPTIMISTIC CLAIM SAFETY

Allocator entries are hints. Atomic create-if-absent is the race primitive.

For portfolio work:
`next_generation = pin_generation + 1`
`claim_path = coordination/portfolio/pins/<job_id>/G<next_generation_6d>.json`

For normal opportunities:
`claim_path = coordination/opportunities/claims/<opportunity_id>.json`

Do not pre-read those directories. CREATE first.

After winning, validate exact current job state before substantive mutation. If the allocator hint became stale, do no substantive mutation; write a bounded stale-hint abort/return and immediately re-enter fast allocation.

Ready unowned work outranks recovery because it is cheaper and less ambiguous. Recovery is attempted only after clean ready work is exhausted.

If allocator age is >90s, skip recovery instead of manually reconstructing liveness.

## AFTER OWNERSHIP

Now load only what the exact job needs, including when applicable:
- portfolio PIN + worker contract;
- Guide/Metabolism for claimed guide work;
- verification/critic controls;
- Master Context for strategic/root work;
- page plate/request/publication laws for `AAA000` scope;
- Live Page Watch only for human-visible page changes;
- `coordination/efficiency/EFFICIENCY_RATCHET_V1.md` + `RATCHET_BASELINE_V1.json` ONLY when the claimed job changes a coordination hot path, allocator, worker bootstrap, Guide routing, Live publication/projection, page publication pipeline, or is itself an efficiency/rescate job.

Then:
- execute through definition of done;
- re-fetch/CAS mutable targets;
- heartbeat during longer work;
- RETURN durably with evidence/tests/changed paths/residuals;
- materialize grounded successors when authorized;
- re-enter fast allocation in the SAME chat after RETURN.

## EFFICIENCY RATCHET

Known efficiency wins are cumulative durable constraints, not chat memory.

If owned work touches a hot path protected by the ratchet:
- preserve every existing ratchet invariant unless a replacement is measurably better;
- run `node scripts/check-efficiency-ratchet.mjs .` before returning when the environment permits;
- if the work reveals a new repeated-waste pattern, add a new durable ratchet item + regression check instead of only patching the local symptom;
- never weaken/delete a guard merely to make a new design pass;
- prefer compiler/static/CI fixes over spawning workers to repair wasted workers.

The runtime telemetry projection is `gh-pages:live/efficiency.json`. A sustained regression is one system bottleneck and should converge to one deduplicated `GUIDE_RESCATE`/critic route, not one repair task per failed worker.

## GUIDE / RESCATE

Guide is a worker role, not a privileged chat. A claimed guide job may be `GUIDE_PLANNER`, `GUIDE_INTEGRATOR`, `GUIDE_RESCATE`, `GUIDE_CRITIC` or `GUIDE_STEWARD`.

Guide work must change durable reality, not just analyse. `RESCATE` means remove a bottleneck/connect a cable/make work claimable/reduce duplication or human routing.

When a Guide/Rescate worker changes a known hot path or discovers structural coordination waste, the Efficiency Ratchet applies after ownership. The repair is incomplete if the same regression can silently return on the next protocol rewrite.

Do not invent filler because capacity exceeds useful work. Surplus capacity ends quickly in `NO_ALLOCATION`.

## RECOVERY

Recovery applies only to previously owned work:
- no PIN/claim -> no recovery;
- <6m latest owned signal -> active;
- 6–10m -> suspect;
- >=10m + retry-safe -> recovery candidate;
- newest valid pin generation is authoritative.

## SUCCESS

Healthy worker:
`BEACON -> allocator -> CREATE -> STARTED -> WORK -> RETURN -> REALLOCATE`

Surplus worker:
`BEACON -> <=3 CREATE attempts -> NO_ALLOCATION -> STOP`

No multi-minute `Buscando trabajo`. No worker swarm repairing workers that never owned anything.

Long-term rule: a discovered coordination optimization must become easier to preserve than to accidentally undo.
